---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CoastFiCalculator from '../../components/calculators/CoastFiCalculator.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/layout/ContactBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Coast FI / Net Worth Calculator"
  description="A planning model that connects today's savings, future contributions, and investment growth to retirement targets."
  canonicalPath="/work/coast-fi"
>
  <article class="coast-page">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <h1>Coast FI / Net Worth Calculator</h1>
      <p class="case-hero__premise">A planning model that connects today’s savings, future contributions, and investment growth to retirement targets.</p>
      <p class="case-hero__lede">I started with a detailed retirement-planning spreadsheet, then audited it and turned the Coast FI part into a simpler four-mode web calculator.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="calculator-stage">
      <CoastFiCalculator />
    </div>

    <section class="story-section story-section--split" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
      <div class="story-copy">
        <p class="section-kicker">Original model</p>
        <h2 id="origin-title">It started as a much bigger spreadsheet.</h2>
        <p>I originally built a four-sheet retirement-planning model that tracked contributions every paycheque across 41 years. It handled TFSA and RRSP contribution allocation, modeled RRSP refunds, non-registered investing, FHSA tracking, and annual net worth and Coast FI calculations.</p>
        <p>That level of detail was useful for my own scenario planning, but it was too specific for a public tool. For the website, I pulled out the Coast FI question and rebuilt it around a much smaller set of assumptions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
        <p class="architecture__label" id="architecture-title">Original model architecture</p>
        <p class="architecture__flowline">Inputs + contribution plan → 1,066 bi-weekly periods → TFSA → RRSP → refund recycling → non-registered → Account growth + FHSA tracking → Annual net worth + Coast FI</p>
        <p class="architecture__support">Working at the pay-period level let the model track account room, contributions, refunds, and balances as they changed over time rather than relying on one annual savings assumption.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section refactor-section" aria-labelledby="refactor-title">
      <div class="section-heading-block">
        <p class="section-kicker">Product redesign</p>
        <h2 id="refactor-title">Making the public version simpler</h2>
        <p>The full spreadsheet had more detail than a public Coast FI calculator needed. Not everyone needs a detailed engine with TFSA and RRSP waterfall options, RRSP refund recycling, and non-registered spillover tracking to answer a general retirement question. For the web version, I kept the inputs required for the Coast calculation and removed the account-specific mechanics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="refactor-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Retained in the public tool</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Current invested portfolio</li>
            <li>Retirement portfolio target</li>
            <li>Current age and retirement age</li>
            <li>Expected real annual return</li>
            <li>Coast threshold</li>
            <li>Constant real monthly contributions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Deliberately removed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Account-specific tax treatment</li>
            <li>TFSA/RRSP contribution-room mechanics</li>
            <li>RRSP refund recycling</li>
            <li>FHSA withdrawal logic</li>
            <li>Pension details</li>
            <li>Non-registered tax-drag assumptions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section testing-section" aria-labelledby="testing-title">
      <div class="section-heading-block">
        <p class="section-kicker">Testing</p>
        <h2 id="testing-title">Checking the web model</h2>
        <p class="proof-line">34 regression tests · 34 passed · 0 failed</p>
        <p>To check the web calculator independently, I built a separate Python implementation to generate expected outputs, then compared those against the TypeScript engine across 34 normal and edge cases. The tests covered all four calculator modes, zero and negative returns, portfolios already above the Coast threshold, unreachable targets, and invalid inputs. All 34 passed.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section workbook-section" aria-labelledby="workbook-title">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Workbook</p>
        <h2 id="workbook-title">Download the sanitized workbook</h2>
        <p>The demonstration workbook uses hypothetical values and shows the deeper bi-weekly model behind the project. It is separate from the simplified web calculator.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="workbook-download" href="/downloads/Coast_FI_Calculator_Public_Sanitized.xlsx" download>
        <span>
          <strong>Download workbook</strong>
          <small>XLSX · hypothetical inputs</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section limits-section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <div class="limits-copy">
        <p class="section-kicker">Limitations</p>
        <h2 id="limits-title">What the calculator leaves out</h2>
        <p>The calculator assumes a constant real return and constant monthly contributions. It does not model taxes, investment fees, account rules, pensions, withdrawals, or market uncertainty.</p>
        <p>The results are illustrative and for educational purposes only. The math has been refined and tested, but if your Coast plan only works with a 16% real return every year, talk to a fee-only financial planner before you actually stop contributing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <ContactBand />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .coast-page { max-width: var(--content-wide); margin-inline: auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.75rem) clamp(1.125rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) clamp(5.25rem, 8vw, 7.5rem); }
  .case-hero, .story-section { max-width: var(--content-main); margin-inline: auto; }
  .case-hero { padding-bottom: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6.5rem); }
  .case-hero h1 { max-width: 64rem; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3.15rem, 7vw, 6.5rem); line-height: .96; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
  .case-hero__premise { max-width: 55rem; margin: 1.45rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.38; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .case-hero__lede { max-width: 45rem; margin: 1.35rem 0 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .calculator-stage { max-width: var(--content-main); margin: 0 auto clamp(6rem, 10vw, 9rem); }
  .section-kicker { margin: 0 0 .8rem; color: var(--color-teal); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 820; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .story-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .story-section h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 4.25rem); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .story-section--split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .82fr) minmax(26rem, 1.18fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem); align-items: start; }
  .story-copy p:not(.section-kicker), .section-heading-block > p:not(.section-kicker), .workbook-section p, .limits-copy p { color: var(--color-text); margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
  .architecture { padding: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 2rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-card); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .architecture__label { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .11em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .architecture__flowline { margin: 0; color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 760; line-height: 1.7; }
  .architecture__support { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); color: var(--color-text); }
  .section-heading-block { max-width: 58rem; }
  .proof-line { color: var(--color-deep-teal) !important; font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.55rem); font-weight: 800; }
  .refactor-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .refactor-grid > div { padding: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-line); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .refactor-grid h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .refactor-grid ul { margin: 1rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .refactor-grid li + li { margin-top: .45rem; }
  .workbook-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(19rem,.6fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: end; }
  .workbook-download { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; min-height: 5rem; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-deep-teal); border-radius: .75rem; color: var(--color-deep-teal); text-decoration: none; }
  .workbook-download strong, .workbook-download small { display: block; }
  .workbook-download small { margin-top: .2rem; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .limits-copy { max-width: var(--content-reading); }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) { .story-section--split, .workbook-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) { .refactor-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 35rem) { .coast-page { padding-inline: 1.125rem; } .case-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 4.4rem); } }
</style>
